    "body": "## Fix PR closed without merging\n\nPR #11824 (the `hookTimeout` bump) was closed by @yuki-takei with this reasoning:\n\n> Closing without merging.\n>\n> On review, this only widened the failure-detection window around the contention rather than addressing it \u2014 `app-integration`'s sibling hook (`test/setup/migrate-mongo.ts`) already had its `hookTimeout` doubled for the same \"environment timing\" reason (#11752) and still flaked under load afterward, which is direct evidence that a bare timeout bump doesn't hold here. The change was also scoped to the whole `app-integration` project's `hookTimeout`, not just the `getInstance()` hook, so it would have quietly widened the failure-detection window for every other hook in every `*.integ.ts` file in that project.\n>\n> Root-cause fix (bounding concurrent worker cold-init instead of widening the timeout) tracked in a follow-up PR against #11820/#11821/#11822.\n\nThis is a fair correction to this run's investigation: #11752's own prior timeout bump for the same \"environment timing\" category, still recurring afterward, is exactly the kind of evidence this skill's Step 3 guardrail asks for before accepting a timeout increase, and it wasn't checked before proposing this fix. Moving this issue back to `phase/under-investigation` \u2014 a maintainer-tracked follow-up PR addressing concurrent cold-init contention (rather than the timeout) is already in progress; no further action needed from this routine unless that follow-up needs review.\n\n---\n*Investigated by Claude Code (autonomous flaky-ci-routine)*\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
