    "updated_at": "2026-08-28T21:05:50Z",
    "body": "Superseding the fix-PR link again: #11826 was closed \u2014 its `vitest.workspace.mts`-based `maxForks` change was silently ignored by Vitest (per-project `poolOptions` in the deprecated workspace-file format do not apply; confirmed by measuring actual CPU usage during a run). All CI verification done against #11826 was unknowingly testing default, uncapped behavior.\n\n#11828 independently fixes the same underlying mechanism (too many concurrent per-file setup-hook invocations on a CI runner) via the correct method \u2014 a CLI flag (`--poolOptions.forks.maxForks=4`) on the `test:integ` script, which actually takes effect. It was written for #11752 (`migrate-mongo.ts`) but covers the same `test:integ` invocation this issue's `getInstance()` cold-init runs under, with real local-repro evidence (80%\u21920% hook-timeout failures under stress) and green CI.\n\n**Fix PR**: https://github.com/growilabs/growi/pull/11828\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
