    "body": "### Additional observation (genuine recurrence after claimed fix \u2014 reopened, escalated to confirmed)\n\n- Run: https://github.com/growilabs/growi/actions/runs/33650470894\n- Job: ci-app-test-integration (24.x, 8.0, 8, 8.19.16)\n- Commit: a5b8ac8c81fd035144a0d0c7948b53fe690081ca\n- Date: 2026-09-02T15:43:58Z\n\n```\nFAIL   app-integration  src/server/service/page/v5.non-public-page.integ.ts > PageService page operations with non-public pages\nError: Hook timed out in 10000ms.\nIf this is a long-running hook, pass a timeout value as the last argument or configure it globally with \"hookTimeout\".\n \u276f src/server/service/page/v5.non-public-page.integ.ts:181:3\n    181|   beforeAll(async () => {\n       |   ^\n    182|     crowi = await getInstance();\n```\n\nThis commit (2026-09-02T15:43:58Z) is well **after** #11828's merge (2026-08-28T21:37:26Z, `--poolOptions.forks.maxForks=4`). This run also carried 6 fresh occurrences of the sibling `test/setup/migrate-mongo.ts` hook timeout (see #11752, same commit) in the same job \u2014 i.e. `maxForks=4` mitigated but did not eliminate the underlying per-worker cold-init contention this fix targeted. Escalating straight to `flaky/confirmed` per detect-flaky-ci's reopened-issue rule (a recurrence after a claimed fix outweighs a first-time observation).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
