    "body": "### Investigation \u2014 root cause identified, confidence gate: MEDIUM (stop for human decision)\n\n**Category (Step 3)**: same underlying mechanism as #11752 \u2014 Environment timing / Driver 2, with a concrete structural cause, not just runner contention.\n\n**Root cause**: `test/setup/crowi.ts`'s `getInstance()` uses a module-level `let _instance: Crowi | null = null` singleton, intended to initialize once per worker (full `Crowi` cold-init: models, config manager, Socket.IO, passport, ACL, page/notification/activity/user-group services \u2014 a genuinely heavy sequence). This is the exact same pattern as `migrate-mongo.ts`'s `migrationsRun` flag (#11752), and it has the same bug: Vitest's default `isolate: true` for the `app-integration` project resets the module registry **per test file**, so `_instance` never survives past the file that first set it \u2014 every one of the ~270 `*.integ.ts` files across `app-integration`/`app-integration-exclusive` pays a full `Crowi` cold-init, not once per worker as the singleton pattern assumes.\n\n**A precedent for the real fix already exists in this exact config file.** `apps/app/vitest.workspace.mts`'s `app-integration-vault` project (lines ~146-178) already sets `isolate: false` for precisely this class of problem \u2014 its own comment says: \"isolate=false reuses the module cache across files so mongoose model registrations (Comment, Page, etc.) are not re-executed and conflict.\" `app-integration` and `app-integration-exclusive` (where `crowi.ts` and `migrate-mongo.ts` live) do **not** set `isolate: false` \u2014 that's the gap. With `isolate: false` (without `vault`'s `singleFork`, so `maxForks=4` parallelism is preserved), each of the (up to 4) forked workers would keep its own persistent module registry across the files it runs, making `getInstance()` and `migrationsRun` actually behave \"once per worker\" as both were designed to.\n\nThis same finding also very likely explains why `test/setup/mongo/index.ts`'s own `beforeAll` guard (\"Skip if already connected... connection persists per worker\") never actually skips today \u2014 under `isolate: true`, `mongoose` itself is a fresh module instance per file, so `mongoose.connection.readyState` never carries over either. All three \"once per worker\" setup files in this project(`mongo/index.ts`, `migrate-mongo.ts`, `crowi.ts`) share the identical false premise.\n\n**Why MEDIUM, not HIGH**: `isolate: false` is a project-wide behavioral change (affects every file in `app-integration`/`app-integration-exclusive`, ~270 files), not a 1-2 file fix. It trades away Vitest's per-file module reset, which is also a safety net against cross-file state leakage (Crowi service caches, mongoose model state, any test that implicitly relies on a fresh module graph without calling `resetInstance()`). Confirming it's safe needs a real, full run of the `app-integration`/`app-integration-exclusive` suites, not just log analysis \u2014 exactly the kind of verification this skill's guardrail asks for before treating a structural test-infra change as HIGH confidence.\n\n**Recommendation for a human**: evaluate `isolate: false` for `app-integration` and `app-integration-exclusive` (mirroring `app-integration-vault`), verified by a full local/CI run of both projects checking for newly-surfaced cross-file state leakage, as a single fix that would very likely resolve #11752 and this issue together (and prevent this whole class of \"silently degrades from per-worker to per-file\" bug from recurring in a fourth setup file later). This is a companion finding to the `globalSetup`-based fix already proposed for #11752 \u2014 either approach (or both) addresses the same class of defect; a human should decide which is preferable given the blast radius.\n\nNo code change made this run \u2014 pausing this issue per this routine's autonomous-mode policy for MEDIUM-confidence gates; continuing with the rest of the queue.\n\n---\n*Investigated by Claude Code (autonomous flaky-ci-routine)*\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
